### File Upload Pages (Rapid Prototyping)

For rapid prototyping, file upload pages can bypass validation to allow quick testing:

- **Controller**: Accept empty submissions and store placeholder values
- **Template**: Remove `enctype="multipart/form-data"` attribute to avoid 415 errors without multipart parsing plugin

Example controller pattern:

```javascript
export const postUploadController = {
  handler(request, h) {
    const application = request.yar.get('application') || {}
    application.uploadedFile =
      request.payload.uploadedFile || 'uploaded-file-placeholder'
    request.yar.set('application', application)
    return h.redirect(ROUTES.NEXT_PAGE)
  }
}
```

Example template (no enctype):

```njk
<form method="post" novalidate>
  {{ govukFileUpload({ ... }) }}
  {{ govukButton({ text: "Continue" }) }}
</form>
```

This allows the journey to continue without configuring file upload handling.

## Common Structural Mistakes

### Wrong Template Paths (Causes 500 Errors)

❌ `return h.view('start', { ... })`
✅ `return h.view('journey-name/start', { ... })`

Always use `{journey-name}/{template-name}` format. See [nunjucks.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/nunjucks.mdc).

### Missing POST Routes

Every form needs both GET (display) and POST (submit) routes registered in `index.js`.

### Plugin Not Registered

Journey plugin must be registered in [src/server/router.js](mdc:src/server/router.js) or routes won't work.

### Missing ROUTES Object on Summary

Summary template needs entire `ROUTES` object passed from controller, not individual route strings.

### Missing Guard Redirects

Summary and confirmation pages must check session data and redirect to start if missing.

### File Upload Forms Causing 415 Errors

❌ **Using multipart form data without plugin:**

```njk
<form method="post" novalidate enctype="multipart/form-data">
```

✅ **For rapid prototyping, remove enctype:**

```njk
<form method="post" novalidate>
```

Hapi.js requires a plugin (like `@hapi/inert` or multipart parser) to handle `enctype="multipart/form-data"`. For rapid prototyping, remove the enctype attribute and accept placeholder values in the controller.

### Nested Session Data Access

❌ **Reading from wrong location:**

```javascript
hotelCount: application.hotelCount
hmoCount: application.hmoCount
```

✅ **Access nested objects correctly:**

```javascript
const roomCounts = application.roomCounts || {}
hotelCount: roomCounts.hotelCount
hmoCount: roomCounts.hmoCount
```

**Pattern**: When storing related data, group in nested objects (e.g., `roomCounts`, `roomDetails`) and access via the nested path in both GET controllers (for displaying) and POST controllers (for saving).

### Conditional Back Links Based on User Selections

Back links may need to be conditional based on previous user choices:

❌ **Hardcoded back link:**

```javascript
backLink: ROUTES.UPLOAD_REDLINE
```

✅ **Conditional back link based on user journey:**

```javascript
const backLink = application.hasRedlineBoundaryFile
  ? ROUTES.UPLOAD_REDLINE
  : application.redlineBoundaryPolygon
    ? ROUTES.MAP
    : ROUTES.REDLINE_MAP
```

**Pattern**: Calculate back links dynamically based on session data to reflect the actual path the user took through the journey.

### Exit Pages Need Back Links

Exit pages (no-edp, non-residential, etc.) must have back links to allow users to return:

❌ **Exit page without back link:**

```javascript
export const exitPageController = {
  handler(_request, h) {
    return h.view('journey-name/exit', { heading: 'Exit' })
  }
}
```

✅ **Exit page with conditional back link:**

```javascript
export const exitPageController = {
  handler(request, h) {
    const application = request.yar.get('application') || {}
    const backLink = application.previousPage || ROUTES.START

    return h.view('journey-name/exit', {
      heading: 'Exit',
      backLink
    })
  }
}
```

**Pattern**: All pages except start must have back links, including exit/conditional pages.

### Email Content Pages Must Use Session Data

Email content pages should retrieve data from session, not use placeholder objects:

❌ **Using placeholder data:**

```javascript
export const emailContentController = {
  handler(_request, h) {
    return h.view('journey-name/email-content', {
      data: { estimateReference: 'PLACEHOLDER' }
    })
  }
}
```

✅ **Retrieve from session:**

```javascript
export const emailContentController = {
  handler(request, h) {
    const application = request.yar.get('application') || {}
    const applicant = request.yar.get('applicant') || {}

    return h.view('journey-name/email-content', {
      data: {
        estimateReference: application.estimateReference,
        email: applicant.email
        // ... other session data
      }
    })
  }
}
```

**Pattern**: Email content and similar display pages should retrieve actual session data, not use hardcoded placeholders.

### Missing Journey Links on Home Page

Every new journey should have a link added to the home page table in `src/server/home/index.njk`:

```njk
<tr class="govuk-table__row">
  <td class="govuk-table__cell">
    <a href="/journey-name/start" class="govuk-link">Journey Name</a>
  </td>
  <td class="govuk-table__cell">
    Journey description here.
  </td>
</tr>
```

Add after the existing journey rows in the table body.

## Validation Checklist

Before completing a journey:

**Setup**

- [ ] Plugin registered in `src/server/router.js`
- [ ] Journey link added to home page (if needed)

**Navigation**

- [ ] All pages have back links (except start)
- [ ] Back links point to correct previous page
- [ ] Summary has Change links with ROUTES object passed
- [ ] Change links return users to summary after updating (unless conditional logic requires intermediate pages)
- [ ] All links use ROUTES constants (not hardcoded paths)
- [ ] Template paths use correct journey-name/template format
- [ ] Journey link added to home page table (src/server/home/index.njk)

**Forms & Validation**

- [ ] Forms use `method="post" novalidate"`
- [ ] POST controllers validate input
- [ ] Errors flash and redirect back to form
- [ ] Error summary displayed when errors present
- [ ] Field-level errors shown on inputs

**Session Management**

- [ ] POST controllers save data with `request.yar.set()`
- [ ] GET controllers retrieve data with `request.yar.get()`
- [ ] Summary retrieves all data from session
- [ ] Confirmation clears session with `request.yar.reset()`
- [ ] Summary/confirmation have guard redirects

**Content Accuracy**

- [ ] All page titles match specification exactly
- [ ] All form labels match specification exactly
- [ ] All error messages match specification word-for-word
- [ ] All button text matches specification exactly
- [ ] Dynamic content uses actual session data (not static values)
- [ ] Email content pages retrieve data from session (not placeholders)
- [ ] Nested session data accessed correctly (e.g., `application.roomCounts.hotelCount`)
- [ ] Back links are conditional based on user's journey path (when applicable)
- [ ] Exit pages have back links to allow users to return

